## PART A — THE DIRECTION

### A1 — SETTLED ALREADY? **No slug.**
Decided, not settled-elsewhere: `docs/cycle27-plan.md:1600-1604` (45(f)) defines S3a, `STATUS.md:74` orders it as the second act. Citing a plan's own decision back at it would block every planned build — the reasoning the cycle-57 review used and the judgement session accepted.

### A2 — REFUTED ALREADY? **No slug.**
The one standing refutation — 38(g) semantics, a top-level indicator wired out of `#637` making a loop-border tunnel — was disposed `FIXED: refuted-already` (`archive/peer/2026-09-20-priorart-d1-s3a-focus-ind.md:362`) and then measured away twice: `#637` **59→59 terminals, 48→48 wired, no tunnel, no border object** (`tools/bench/diag_s57_ctmove_wire.log:64`; `tools/bench/diag_s58_boolwire.log:159-160`). The recipe inherits `move_in`-into-`#639` as mandatory. Nothing else argues against this build.

### A3 — CONTRADICTED → `contradicted`
**45(c) asserts the S3a wiring survives the 1.2 move, and cites for it the item that measured the opposite.**

> `docs/cycle27-plan.md:1588-1589` — *"When 1.2 is built later the indicator terminals move with their source nodes (one node per `move_in`, **37(d)**); the local variables in 1.5 need no change."*

against

> `docs/cycle27-plan.md:1093` (37(d)) — *"`move_in` **TAKES ONE NODE PER CALL AND SEVERS EVERY WIRE ON IT, IN EITHER ORDER** — there is no 'move the set and keep its internal wires'."*
> `docs/cycle27-plan.md:843` (33(a)) — *"A move severs the node's wires; the relocated node lands in the new body **unwired**."*

Both S3a sources are booked for that move: `docs/d1-build-plan.md:295` — **`10757 … → 1.2`**; `:304` — **`10686 … → 1.2`**. Each indicator is a **branch of its source's own net** (numeric 10990, boolean 10799, whole-VI `Wire` delta 0 — `tools/bench/diag_s58_boolwire.log:153`), so severing the source takes the indicator's only feed with it.

**This changes no line of the recipe.** What is false is the durability clause: when 1.2 is built both indicators go bare, the 1.2 stage owes two re-wire rows no document lists, and until they land loop 1.5 reads an indicator nothing writes. Disposition is one sentence in 45(c).

